sntpd (3.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * The SERVER argument is now repeatable and acts as a failover list,
    with per-server iburst and prefer options
  * Every address a server name resolves to is tried in turn
  * IPv6 literal addresses can now be given on the command line
  * New -m option, the minimum poll interval
  * Kiss-o'-Death handling, RFC 4330 section 8
  * RFC 4330 cross-checks are now enabled by default in daemon mode
  * Fix --enable-debug build, and select() now watches every socket

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:39:00 +0200

sntpd (3.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Improved log messages on failure to resolve DNS names
  * On failure to do DNS lookup, bind(), or connect(), sntpd now properly
    handle SIGTERM and its 1 sec retry is not as chatty in the log
  * Update co-author's last name

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Sun, 13 Mar 2022 11:02:38 +0100

sntpd (3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * New name for project and new version.
  * Initial support for a very limited server mode, enabled by default
  * Move adjtimex to its own .deb file, provided by other packages too
  * Stripped down command line options, compared to ntpclient
  * Separate ntpclient binary no longer available, though can be invoked
    by symlinking to sntpd if needed (not enabled by default)
  * Fix spelling errors in man page found by lintian

 -- Joachim Nilsson <troglobit@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Mar 2020 10:32:53 +0100

